"""
DEFINING REST ADDRESSES

Query:
/releases/ueproxy-...
/services/                     - here are PIDs
/artifactories/                - they are not ueproxy bound
/access_layers/

Resource creation:
POST /ueproxy/releases/  (POST has file ueproxy-0.7.0-py38-macos_10.9.pyz)  will upload ueproxy-0.7.0-py38-macos_10.9.pyz
                         - will take format from file extension
POST /releases/ueproxy-0.7.0-py38-macos_10.9?format=pyz&method=pip  will download ueproxy-0.7.0-py38-macos_10.9.pyz from some Artifactory using pip
                                                                    (Artifactory URL is resource)
POST /ueproxy/artifactories/  register URL (in post data) for specific type of Artifactory (for pip, for docker, ...; default & alternatives)

POST /ueproxy/access_layers/  will upload taf.ue.proxy.access.android.tgz pkg version stored inside; metadata may carry info
                              "which ueproxy ver it will work with"; preinstall into such venv?

# https://www.oreilly.com/library/view/restful-web-services/9780596529260/ch04.html#id382583
# Overloaded POST: The not-so-uniform interface - overloads action - not only create-or-append
# it is sometimes allowed/necessary to do this small RPC-style but you should avoid it as much as possible in RESTfull design
# Fortunately, in our case it is POST(a) - it appends new process/PID to running services, resource is 'result of POST action'
POST /ueproxy/services/  start ueproxy service using specified release and access-layer-version
# We may limit it to "single process allowed" or - in future - allow multiple
# for multiple processes UE ownership, reservation issue appears - not enough to keep it in process memory; need persistence (DB)
POST data - raw HTTP:  Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
                                     release=0.7.0-py38-macos_10.9.pyz&al=taf.ue.proxy.access.android&alver=0.8.2&restart=false
POST data - JSON:   {'release': '0.7.0-py38-macos_10.9.pyz', 'al': 'taf.ue.proxy.access.android', 'alver': '0.8.2', 'restart': false, 'port': 'auto'}
POST data - JSON:   {'release': '0.7.0', 'python': '3.8', 'os': 'macos_10.9', 'al': 'taf.ue.proxy.access.android',
                     'alver': '0.8.2', 'restart': false, 'port': 'auto'}
# run ue-proxy service based on docker image
POST data - JSON:   {'release': '0.7.0', 'format': 'docker', 'python': '3.8', 'os': 'macos_10.9',
                     'al': 'taf.ue.proxy.access.android', 'alver': '0.8.2', 'restart': false, 'port': 'auto'}

DELETE /ueproxy/services/{pid}  will stop ue-proxy service running inside process of given pid
PUT /ueproxy/services/{pid}     restart ue-proxy service if it is running under given pid (CAUTION: restarted will get new pid)
"""


